## 5. Data

```yaml id=DATA kind=data
entities:
  - id: ENT-User
    name: User
    plain_name: Customers and providers
    fields:
      - {name: name}
      - {name: phone}
      - {name: email, required: false}
      - {name: avatar, type: image, required: false}
      - {name: created_at, type: datetime}
    seed_guidance: Two sample customers and two provider accounts with names that match the app locale.
  - id: ENT-Address
    name: Address
    plain_name: Saved addresses
    fields:
      - {name: user, type: ref, ref: ENT-User}
      - {name: label, description: 'Home, Work, ...'}
      - {name: line1}
      - {name: line2, required: false}
      - {name: city}
      - {name: postal_code}
      - {name: latitude, type: number, required: false, description: From the map pin}
      - {name: longitude, type: number, required: false, description: From the map pin}
      - {name: access_notes, required: false, description: 'Gate code, floor, parking'}
      - {name: is_default, type: bool}
  - id: ENT-ServiceCategory
    name: Service category
    plain_name: Service categories
    fields:
      - {name: name}
      - {name: image, type: image, required: false}
    seed_guidance: Three to five categories that fit the business, for example hair, skin, wellness.
  - id: ENT-Service
    name: Service
    plain_name: Services
    fields:
      - {name: category, type: ref, ref: ENT-ServiceCategory}
      - {name: name}
      - {name: description, type: text}
      - {name: duration_minutes, type: int}
      - {name: price, type: money}
      - {name: image, type: image, required: false}
      - {name: location_kind, type: enum, enum: LocationKind}
      - {name: is_active, type: bool}
    seed_guidance: 10 to 20 services with durations from 15 to 120 minutes and a mix of venue, at-customer
      and online services.
  - id: ENT-Provider
    name: Provider
    plain_name: Providers
    fields:
      - {name: name}
      - {name: title, required: false, description: For example Senior stylist}
      - {name: bio, type: text}
      - {name: photo, type: image}
      - {name: rating, type: number, required: false}
      - {name: rating_count, type: int, required: false}
      - {name: years_experience, type: int, required: false}
      - {name: languages, type: json, required: false}
      - {name: location_name}
      - {name: city}
    seed_guidance: Four to eight providers, each offering three to six of the services.
  - id: ENT-ProviderService
    name: Provider service
    plain_name: What each provider offers
    fields:
      - name: provider
        type: ref
        ref: ENT-Provider
      - name: service
        type: ref
        ref: ENT-Service
      - name: price
        type: money
        required: false
        description: Only when it differs from the service price
    source: research
  - id: ENT-Slot
    name: Slot
    plain_name: Available times
    fields:
      - {name: provider, type: ref, required: false, ref: ENT-Provider}
      - {name: starts_at, type: datetime}
      - {name: ends_at, type: datetime}
      - {name: is_available, type: bool}
    seed_guidance: Hourly or half-hourly slots for the next 14 days with realistic gaps, some already
      taken.
  - id: ENT-Booking
    name: Booking
    plain_name: Bookings
    fields:
      - {name: user, type: ref, ref: ENT-User}
      - {name: service, type: ref, ref: ENT-Service}
      - {name: provider, type: ref, required: false, ref: ENT-Provider}
      - {name: status, type: enum, enum: BookingStatus}
      - {name: starts_at, type: datetime}
      - {name: ends_at, type: datetime}
      - {name: location_kind, type: enum, enum: LocationKind}
      - {name: address, type: ref, required: false, ref: ENT-Address}
      - {name: notes, type: text, required: false}
      - {name: price, type: money}
      - {name: payment_method, type: enum, required: false, enum: PaymentMethodType}
      - {name: reference, description: Short booking code shown to the customer}
      - {name: created_at, type: datetime}
      - {name: cancel_reason, required: false}
    state_machine:
      field: status
      states: [requested, confirmed, completed, cancelled, no_show]
      transitions:
        - {from: requested, target: confirmed, 'on': confirm}
        - {from: confirmed, target: completed, 'on': complete}
        - {from: confirmed, target: no_show, 'on': mark_no_show}
        - {from: requested, target: cancelled, 'on': cancel}
        - {from: confirmed, target: cancelled, 'on': cancel}
    seed_guidance: Four sample bookings for the main customer, covering upcoming confirmed, requested,
      completed and cancelled.
  - id: ENT-ReminderPreference
    name: Reminder preference
    plain_name: Reminder settings
    fields:
      - name: user
        type: ref
        ref: ENT-User
      - name: enabled
        type: bool
      - name: lead_minutes
        type: int
        description: How long before the booking, for example 60 or 1440
      - name: channel
        type: enum
        enum: ReminderChannel
    source: research
enums:
  - {name: BookingStatus, values: [requested, confirmed, completed, cancelled, no_show]}
  - {name: LocationKind, values: [at_venue, at_customer, online]}
  - {name: PaymentMethodType, values: [card, wallet, pay_at_venue]}
  - {name: ReminderChannel, values: [push, sms, email]}
seed_guidance: Generate sample records that read like a real business, in the language of the app.
```

## 6. API

```yaml id=API kind=api
operations:
  - id: API-requestOtp
    name: Request sign-in code
    method: POST
    path: /auth/otp
    request_entity: ENT-User
    notes: Sends a one-time code to the phone number. Mock sender in the preview.
  - id: API-verifyOtp
    name: Verify sign-in code
    method: POST
    path: /auth/otp/verify
    request_entity: ENT-User
    response_entity: ENT-User
    notes: Returns the session. New phone numbers create a user.
  - id: API-getMe
    name: Get my profile
    method: GET
    path: /me
    response_entity: ENT-User
    auth: authenticated
  - id: API-updateMe
    name: Update my profile
    method: PATCH
    path: /me
    request_entity: ENT-User
    response_entity: ENT-User
    auth: authenticated
  - id: API-listAddresses
    name: List my addresses
    method: GET
    path: /addresses
    response_entity: ENT-Address
    response_many: true
    auth: authenticated
  - id: API-createAddress
    name: Add an address
    method: POST
    path: /addresses
    request_entity: ENT-Address
    response_entity: ENT-Address
    auth: authenticated
  - id: API-updateAddress
    name: Change an address
    method: PUT
    path: /addresses/{id}
    request_entity: ENT-Address
    response_entity: ENT-Address
    auth: authenticated
  - id: API-deleteAddress
    name: Delete an address
    method: DELETE
    path: /addresses/{id}
    auth: authenticated
  - id: API-listCategories
    name: List service categories
    method: GET
    path: /categories
    response_entity: ENT-ServiceCategory
    response_many: true
  - id: API-listServices
    name: List services
    method: GET
    path: /services
    response_entity: ENT-Service
    response_many: true
    notes: 'Query: category, q, sort, page.'
  - id: API-getService
    name: Get a service
    method: GET
    path: /services/{id}
    response_entity: ENT-Service
  - id: API-listProviders
    name: List providers
    method: GET
    path: /providers
    response_entity: ENT-Provider
    response_many: true
    notes: 'Query: service, sort, page.'
    source: research
  - id: API-getProvider
    name: Get a provider
    method: GET
    path: /providers/{id}
    response_entity: ENT-Provider
    notes: Includes what they offer (ENT-ProviderService).
    source: research
  - id: API-listSlots
    name: List available times
    method: GET
    path: /slots
    response_entity: ENT-Slot
    response_many: true
    notes: 'Query: service, provider (optional), date. Without a provider the slots of any provider are
      merged.'
  - id: API-createBooking
    name: Create a booking
    method: POST
    path: /bookings
    request_entity: ENT-Booking
    response_entity: ENT-Booking
    auth: authenticated
    notes: Holds the slot. Refuses a slot that was just taken.
  - id: API-listBookings
    name: List my bookings
    method: GET
    path: /bookings
    response_entity: ENT-Booking
    response_many: true
    auth: authenticated
    notes: 'Query: when (upcoming or past).'
  - id: API-getBooking
    name: Get a booking
    method: GET
    path: /bookings/{id}
    response_entity: ENT-Booking
    auth: authenticated
  - id: API-rescheduleBooking
    name: Move a booking
    method: POST
    path: /bookings/{id}/reschedule
    request_entity: ENT-Booking
    response_entity: ENT-Booking
    auth: authenticated
    notes: Allowed only before the cancellation cutoff.
    source: research
  - id: API-cancelBooking
    name: Cancel a booking
    method: POST
    path: /bookings/{id}/cancel
    response_entity: ENT-Booking
    auth: authenticated
    source: research
  - id: API-getReminderPreference
    name: Get my reminder settings
    method: GET
    path: /reminders
    response_entity: ENT-ReminderPreference
    auth: authenticated
    source: research
  - id: API-updateReminderPreference
    name: Change my reminder settings
    method: PUT
    path: /reminders
    request_entity: ENT-ReminderPreference
    response_entity: ENT-ReminderPreference
    auth: authenticated
    source: research
mock_guidance: A generated mock backend answers every operation; nothing leaves the device in the preview.
```

## 7. Roles

```yaml id=ROLES kind=roles
roles:
  - {id: ROLE-customer, name: Customer, description: 'Finds services, books and pays.'}
```

## 8. Integrations

```yaml id=INTEGRATIONS kind=integrations
items:
  - id: INT-sms_otp
    name: Sign-in codes by SMS
    purpose: Send one-time codes so people can sign in with a phone number.
    notes: Mock sender prints the code in the preview. A real SMS provider is chosen at release.
  - id: INT-maps
    name: Maps and directions
    purpose: Show the venue or the provider area on a map and give directions.
    notes: Static sample map in the preview. A real map provider key is needed at release.
  - id: INT-reminders
    name: Booking reminders
    purpose: Schedule a reminder before each booking as a notification.
    notes: Shown as an in-app banner at the reminder time in the preview.
    source: research
    research_ref: RA-001
  - id: INT-send_codes_and_reminders_from_the_server
    name: Send codes and reminders from the server
    purpose: Text messages and reminders are sent through a provider API from a server, not from the app.
    source: research
    research_ref: RA-005
```

## 9. Behavior

```yaml id=BEHAVIOR kind=behavior
offline: Basic cache. The last loaded lists and details stay readable without a connection, and changes
  wait on the phone until the connection returns.
deep_links:
  - /bookings/[id]
  - /bookings/[id]/cancel
  - /bookings/[id]/reschedule
  - /providers/[id]
  - /services/[id]
notifications: [account updates]
permission_prompts: ['Location, only while the app is open and only when the person uses a nearby or map
    feature']
error_conventions:
  - Show a plain-language message and a retry action, never a raw error code
  - Keep what the person typed when a request fails
  - Loading, empty, error and offline states come from the screen recipe
  - 'Never log personal data (data classification: internal)'
accessibility:
  - Every control has a text label for screen readers
  - Text meets WCAG AA contrast in light and dark mode
  - Text grows with the phone's font size setting
  - Touch targets are at least 44 by 44 points
```

## 10. Screens

### SCR-001 - /welcome

```yaml id=SCR-001 kind=screen
route: /welcome
recipe: welcome
purpose: Introduce the app to a signed-out visitor and offer to sign in, create an account or look around
flow: FLW-002
sections: [help_hint]
actions:
  - sign_in: {go: SCR-002}
  - create_account: {go: SCR-003}
  - browse_as_guest: {go: SCR-004}
copy:
  cta_guest: See our services
  cta_primary: Sign in
  cta_secondary: Create account
  intro: Introduce the app to a signed-out visitor and offer to sign in, create an account or look around
  title: Book in a few taps
checks:
  - See our services opens the home screen without asking for an account
  - Sign in and Create account open the matching screens
  - 'Everything this screen promises works: introduce the app to a signed-out visitor and offer to sign
    in, create an account or look around'
```

### SCR-002 - /login

```yaml id=SCR-002 kind=screen
route: /login
recipe: login-otp
purpose: Sign in with a phone number and a one-time code
flow: FLW-002
sections: [help_hint]
actions:
  - send_code: {calls: API-requestOtp, on_success: show the code field and start the resend timer}
  - verify_code: {calls: API-verifyOtp, go: SCR-004, on_success: save the session and open the home screen}
  - new_user_setup: {go: SCR-003, on_success: opened instead of home when the number is new}
states:
  wrong_code: {allow: 'retry, and resend after 30 seconds', show: inline error under the code field}
copy:
  cta: Send code
  hint: We will text you a 6-digit code
  intro: Sign in with a phone number and a one-time code
  title: Sign in
checks:
  - A wrong code shows an error and allows another try
  - The resend link stays disabled for 30 seconds after a send
  - 'Everything this screen promises works: sign in with a phone number and a one-time code'
```

### SCR-003 - /signup

```yaml id=SCR-003 kind=screen
route: /signup
recipe: signup
purpose: Finish a new account with a name and an optional email after the phone number is verified
sections: [help_hint]
actions:
  - finish_profile: {calls: API-updateMe, go: SCR-004, on_success: open the home screen}
copy:
  cta: Start booking
  intro: Finish a new account with a name and an optional email after the phone number is verified
  title: Almost there
checks:
  - The name is required and the email is optional
  - 'Everything this screen promises works: finish a new account with a name and an optional email after
    the phone number is verified'
```

### SCR-004 - /home

```yaml id=SCR-004 kind=screen
route: /home
recipe: dashboard
purpose: Show service categories and popular services and lead into booking
flow: FLW-001
data:
  - {bind: API-listCategories, show: [name, image]}
  - {bind: API-listServices(featured), show: [name, image, duration_minutes, price]}
sections: [greeting, categories, popular_services, help_hint]
actions:
  - open_category: {go: SCR-005}
  - open_service: {go: SCR-006}
copy: {intro: Show service categories and popular services and lead into booking, title: Home}
checks:
  - Tapping a category opens the service list filtered to it
  - Tapping a service opens its page
  - 'Everything this screen promises works: show service categories and popular services and lead into
    booking'
```

### SCR-005 - /services

```yaml id=SCR-005 kind=screen
route: /services
recipe: list-with-filters
purpose: List services with search, category filters and sorting
flow: FLW-001
data:
  - bind: API-listServices(category, q, sort)
    show: [name, image, duration_minutes, price, location_kind]
sections: [search_bar, category_chips, sort_control, service_cards, load_more, help_hint]
actions:
  - open_service: {go: SCR-006}
states:
  empty: {action: Clear filters, message: No services match your search}
copy: {intro: 'List services with search, category filters and sorting'}
checks:
  - Each card shows the duration and the price
  - Searching by name narrows the list as the person types
  - 'Everything this screen promises works: list services with search, category filters and sorting'
```

### SCR-006 - /services/[id]

```yaml id=SCR-006 kind=screen
route: /services/[id]
recipe: detail-with-sticky-cta
purpose: Show one service with its duration, price and what to expect, and start booking it
flow: FLW-001
data:
  - bind: API-getService(id)
    show: [name, image, description, duration_minutes, price, location_kind]
sections:
  - gallery
  - title_price_duration
  - description
  - what_to_expect
  - providers_row
  - sticky_cta
  - help_hint
actions:
  - book_now: {go: SCR-009}
  - see_providers: {go: SCR-007}
copy:
  cta: Book now
  intro: Show one service with its duration, price and what to expect, and start booking it
checks:
  - The location kind (at the venue, at your place or online) is shown clearly
  - Book now opens the time picker for this service
  - 'Everything this screen promises works: show one service with its duration, price and what to expect,
    and start booking it'
```

### SCR-007 - /providers

```yaml id=SCR-007 kind=screen
route: /providers
recipe: list-with-filters
purpose: List the providers who offer a service with their rating and next free time
flow: FLW-003
data:
  - bind: API-listProviders(service, sort)
    show: [name, title, photo, rating, rating_count, location_name]
sections: [filter_chips, sort_control, provider_cards, load_more, help_hint]
actions:
  - open_provider: {go: SCR-008}
states:
  empty: {action: Back to services, message: No providers offer this service yet}
copy: {intro: List the providers who offer a service with their rating and next free time}
checks:
  - Sorting by rating puts the highest rated provider first
  - 'Everything this screen promises works: list the providers who offer a service with their rating and
    next free time'
source: research
research_ref: RA-003
```

### SCR-008 - /providers/[id]

```yaml id=SCR-008 kind=screen
route: /providers/[id]
recipe: detail
purpose: Introduce one provider and let the customer book with them
flow: FLW-003
data:
  - bind: API-getProvider(id)
    show:
      - name
      - title
      - photo
      - bio
      - rating
      - rating_count
      - years_experience
      - languages
      - location_name
  - bind: ENT-ProviderService.price
    show: [service, price]
sections: [photo_name_title, rating_summary, bio, services_offered, reviews_preview, help_hint]
actions:
  - book_with_provider: {go: SCR-009}
copy: {intro: Introduce one provider and let the customer book with them}
checks:
  - The price shown for a service is the provider's own price when it differs
  - 'Everything this screen promises works: introduce one provider and let the customer book with them'
source: research
research_ref: RA-003
```

### SCR-009 - /book/time

```yaml id=SCR-009 kind=screen
route: /book/time
recipe: calendar-slot-picker
purpose: Pick a day and a free time for the chosen service
flow: FLW-001
data:
  - {bind: 'API-listSlots(service, provider, date)', show: [starts_at, ends_at, is_available]}
sections: [service_summary, provider_choice, date_strip, slot_grid, continue_cta, help_hint]
actions:
  - choose_provider: {go: SCR-007}
  - continue: {go: SCR-010}
states:
  no_slots: {action: Try another day, message: No times left on this day}
copy:
  cta: Continue
  intro: Pick a day and a free time for the chosen service
  title: Choose a time
checks:
  - Times in the past and already booked times are disabled
  - Times are shown in the customer's local time zone
  - 'Everything this screen promises works: pick a day and a free time for the chosen service'
```

### SCR-010 - /book/review

```yaml id=SCR-010 kind=screen
route: /book/review
recipe: checkout-review
purpose: Review the service, time and place, add a note and confirm the booking
auth: authenticated
flow: FLW-001
data:
  - {bind: ENT-Booking.price, show: [price]}
  - {bind: API-listAddresses, show: [label, line1, city, access_notes, is_default]}
sections:
  - service_summary
  - provider
  - date_time
  - location_or_address
  - notes_input
  - price_breakdown
  - confirm_cta
  - help_hint
actions:
  - choose_address: {go: SCR-018}
  - confirm_booking: {calls: API-createBooking, go: SCR-011, on_success: hold the slot and open the confirmation}
states:
  address_needed: {disable: confirm_booking, show: Add the address where the service happens}
  slot_taken: {action: Pick another time, show: That time was just taken}
copy:
  cta: Confirm booking
  intro: Review the service, time and place, add a note and confirm the booking
  title: Review your booking
checks:
  - An address is required only for at-your-place services
  - If the slot is taken meanwhile the person is sent back to the time picker with a message
  - 'Everything this screen promises works: review the service, time and place, add a note and confirm
    the booking'
```

